{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/620185-need-some-advice-new-to-ctl","id":620185,"title":"Need some advice, new to CtL","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-08T09:51:46-07:00","id":620185,"title":"Need some advice, new to CtL","content":"I played Changeling once way back in the day for a game spanning a summer, but I didn't really know what I was doing. I have played an unhealthily high amount of Mage the Awakening however, so I know general WoD mechanics and lore rather well, I'm just not very experienced with the Lost template. <br /> <br /> Tonight I'm going to a Victorian London Changeling LARP. I'm going to be a mirrorskin of the hound tribunal, hunting both NPC and PC traitors. Dual kith builds are allowed in this setting so long as the setup makes sense from a story perspective. <br /> <br /> My trouble is this: Being a hunter and assassin of changeling traitors is going to require a broad degree of abilities, which I am good at roleplaying, but I'm not sure I can make a good character sheet that will match up with the skills I need to fulfill this job. <br /> <br /> Specifically in terms of merits and contracts, I'm somewhat clueless as to what I should pick and the game is tonight so I'm short on time to read volumes of options and weigh pros/con's. Any advice for merits an skills that would fit well with this concept at character gen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T04:40:52-07:00","id":621082,"title":"","content":"Assassins come in many forms in the world of darkness. Do you hang out at social event and slip something into their drinks? Do you pick them off with a sniper rifle? (Which, I'll add, cool to do to NPCs, terrible to to to PCs). It depends on how you want to go about it. I personally like the Contracts of Separation. 3 through 5 give you a lot for what you have to pay for them. I'd also suggest some Larceny, your martial art of choice (Weaponry, Firearms, athletics, what have you). Perfect Stillness is great for stealth, and of course... stealth is a good skill to have. Rigid Mask is good, as well as Subterfuge (And grab some empathy while you're at it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T11:46:44-07:00","id":624526,"title":"","content":"A few days too late, I know, but Mirrorskin kith suggests you do well at disguise and blending in. Thus, stealth and subterfuge are likely skills and being able to change your appearance can get you close to your target, so I'd recommend brawl and/or weaponry over firearms for combat skills. After that it all depends on personal preference as far as approach and concept. Investigation and streetwise could help when it comes to tracking someone, persuasion or intimidation to taste when it comes to getting leads out of people...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}